# PHSSJ Portal — Cursor Rules (see AGENTS.md, AGENT_MEMORY.md, docs/VERIFIED_STACK.md)

1. Verify First: Read source files before editing; never guess package versions or Gemini model IDs.
2. Modular & Anti-Bloat: Target 200-350 LOC max per file; reuse components/ui/, hooks, and shared services; keep comments brief.
3. Complete Wiring & Edge Cases: Wire features end-to-end into app state, auth, and sync queues; handle empty data, timeouts, 429/quotas, expired/cancelled auth, permissions, duplicates, and partial batch failures.
4. UI Copy - Zero Jargon: Never display technical/AI terms (ingestion, batching, key rotation, OCR pipeline, tokens, dossier, discrepancy audit, A2UI, inference, payload, schema, compiler, telemetry, IndexedDB, Cloud Firestore) in UI copy or toasts.
5. UI Copy - Concise & Plain: Use 1-4 word titles without verbose subtitles; use plain school terms (Student Folders, Documents, Mismatches, Google Drive Import, Skip Already Imported, Reset Data, Student Records, Marksheets, Daily Attendance, Lesson Plans, Exams & Papers).
6. Clean Errors: Pass user-facing error alerts through utils/userMessage.ts (toUserErrorMessage).
